     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Joe<div><br></div><div>I am fiddling around with your d3-heatmap code (which runs great on actual dataset)  but not sure if I fully understand the way shiny uses the output binding. Did make it a point to go through the info in tutorial but need some more hand holding I guess.</div><div><br></div><div>So here is where it gets a bit hazy for me. Following the demo app here: <a href=\"https://github.com/jcheng5/d3-heatmap/blob/master/demo/d3heatmap.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jcheng5/d3-heatmap/blob/master/demo/d3heatmap.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405734488000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3W0BwI96vrjO1BT9-x8769\">https://github.com/jcheng5/d3-heatmap/blob/master/demo/d3heatmap.R</a></div><div><br></div><div>I can see how you are prepping the data in the renderHeatmap function and return a function to output$heatmap which in turn is passed to heatmapOutput function on the client side but not sure I understand the following.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">heatmapOutput </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\"> </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">function</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">outputId</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">{  ## I am assuming outputId here is the function returned by the renderHeatmap</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">  .....</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">  .....</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\"><pre style=\"font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\"><div style=\"padding-left:10px;background-color:rgb(255,255,204)\">tags<span style=\"font-weight:bold\">$</span>div<span>(</span>id<span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span>outputId<span>,</span> class<span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;d3-heatmap&#39;</span><span>) #not sure why that is passed &quot;as-is&quot; to div tag</span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px;background-color:rgb(255,255,204)\"><span>)</span></div></pre></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">}</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div><br></div><div>Could you please help me understand when/how the actual binding code is being utilized inside the heatmapOutput function to render the d3 plot inside the div. I also dont see any common keyword between the binding function and heatmatOutput that would connect these two together but likely I am missing good amount of logic here.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div>-Abhi</div></div>"
